.TH HELPBUOY-SERVERCTL 8 "" "helpbuoy" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
helpbuoy-serverctl \- run helpbuoy-server admin commands on the system server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B helpbuoy-serverctl
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B helpbuoy-serverctl
runs
.BR helpbuoy-server (1)
as the helpbuoy-server system user on the state of the helpbuoy-server service in
.IR /var/lib/helpbuoy-server ,
so the files it writes stay readable by the service. It must be run as root.
The running server picks up changes within a second.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo helpbuoy-serverctl hostkey
sudo helpbuoy-serverctl techie add alice 'ssh\-ed25519 AAAA...'
sudo helpbuoy-serverctl techie list
sudo helpbuoy-serverctl computer list
sudo helpbuoy-serverctl computer remove SHA256:...
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/helpbuoy-server
Listen address of the service.
.TP
.I /var/lib/helpbuoy-server
Host key, techies, registered computers and server.log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR helpbuoy-server (1)
